{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788048077693139013,"compiled_state":{"alias":"defectible-cretinoid-ladybird","assignee":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":8,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"8391478243c6e4bec6ef31f97791ad56d06fe7b264b3be48678ccb36da75d5f1","event_uuid":"ff1aeae4-7f9a-4030-861e-fa0a19bd94cd","position":{"commit_sha":"f362f7e408b8fe7bf6e6c9c7204c40a7b7bf9969","position":"1788045211215655001-ff1aeae4-7f9a-4030-861e-fa0a19bd94cd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"864e01c0f155ab947273fdcb2ce39f44eb7fd7c98f9a8e11e93cc436d63db489","event_uuid":"b84ead0e-2479-45ac-bdcd-4b4ac4db5fbf","position":{"commit_sha":"6c4c045bcaa07163e319df8e54f14dbd30903ef2","position":"1788046250947734868-b84ead0e-2479-45ac-bdcd-4b4ac4db5fbf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"8190295a3bac3b0869695a57cf9b1c27fa29ddea90204dbf61aa1b8bfa986a98","event_uuid":"4ddd4298-0c1c-40b5-96be-6bdeb5750284","position":{"commit_sha":"6c4c045bcaa07163e319df8e54f14dbd30903ef2","position":"1788046254720271842-4ddd4298-0c1c-40b5-96be-6bdeb5750284"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"2176e4d59bb014c1530a122522a774899dccd9cc292f3c2da5be20a3bd09f35c","event_uuid":"f3259a52-0a94-404a-b018-524187294b3b","position":{"commit_sha":"86076d35f4d4f09aed23357e767b4ab08bc61a30","position":"1788046367054894686-f3259a52-0a94-404a-b018-524187294b3b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"02dfcff6e1731ffa289e76ae1cd937ddc9ca54bbc8803b6e14b88f02c1d5a05a","event_uuid":"340eb6f4-552c-44be-9cab-8a464ee5cef1","position":{"commit_sha":"07c3ce39c3363b7cddb15e9a26a8f8cbb582ab4d","position":"1788046389995614805-340eb6f4-552c-44be-9cab-8a464ee5cef1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"c47e10a270a90881c964de7c6a33e871a0fa4bb11bccf33aff87611e58c1a64d","event_uuid":"776ab24b-739f-43ba-9275-3f5cd721ece3","position":{"commit_sha":"f40596377bf20507fbfb68158c69071352bebe2c","position":"1788047702894112510-776ab24b-739f-43ba-9275-3f5cd721ece3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"996f10a1d6f108e442f75cc545393170743ac66c60ffc5e3911a40060fb70ef2","event_uuid":"c7c71447-8e17-4e2c-ac43-0dd63aefe33c","position":{"commit_sha":"dce25018d485cd66fc672da67e57eaab77986fda","position":"1788047753066239029-c7c71447-8e17-4e2c-ac43-0dd63aefe33c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"869939161c5b98718ccc132c323ca0f2757b6cde0180ad148596f01d96e725ec","event_uuid":"b03086d0-5ca9-47b7-b8a9-eb5f0ff30fb6","position":{"commit_sha":"8b2bed6c000528378961e373d6f233fe8e442411","position":"1788048077693139012-b03086d0-5ca9-47b7-b8a9-eb5f0ff30fb6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Phase 1 RCA (rebar-debug) — proven root cause + attribution. STOPPED at exit gate; remediation is a DESIGN DECISION escalated to the operator.\n\nInvestigated on a fresh worktree off origin/main @ 55589c15 (= reported-against commit). NO live Bedrock/gate call was made — the classification path was reproduced entirely locally with an injected/mocked provider. (The claim of THIS bug succeeded with no Bedrock load: a bug is not plan-review claim-gated.)\n\n### Proven mechanism (H1 wins) — throttle → failover → keyless fallback → INDETERMINATE\n\nUnder concurrent multi-session load the SHARED Bedrock account (896586841071/us-east-1) throttles at the ACCOUNT level (TPM/RPM). The frontier chain is `frontier = { model = \"bedrock:opus\", fallback = [{ model = \"anthropic:opus\" }] }` (rebar.toml). The failure taxonomy classifies a plain rate-limit 429 (ThrottlingException) as `WAIT_AND_RETRY` (retryable), and `model_classes.should_fall_back` fails over the chain for every retryable/`CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL` class — so a throttle triggers failover to `anthropic:opus`. In these environments `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is ABSENT, so the anthropic provider raises `TypeError: Could not resolve authentication method…`. `should_fall_back(TypeError)` is False (NEEDS_INVESTIGATION), so pydantic-ai's `FallbackModel` re-raises the bare `TypeError`; `failure.classify_llm_failure` maps an unmatched `TypeError` → `NEEDS_INVESTIGATION` (non-retryable) → the gate emits the hard **INDETERMINATE** verdict (`_cli/_llm_commands._disposition_exit_code`), NOT the retryable exit-11. Because the account is shared, ALL concurrent sessions throttle and fail over at once → **fleet-wide simultaneous INDETERMINATE**.\n\nThe crux: a throttle that SHOULD be a benign retryable exit-11 (\"back off and retry\") is CONVERTED into a hard INDETERMINATE by the failover to a keyless fallback whose terminal auth error masks the retryable primary cause.\n\n### Runtime proof (dynamic hypothesis, proven by execution — not source-reading)\n\nInjected/mocked provider, no real Bedrock call. Full reproducer script content preserved below.\n\n- **Exp A — plain Bedrock throttle (429 rate_limit) ALONE:** `should_fall_back=True`; verdict = **EXIT_11_RETRYABLE** (`WAIT_AND_RETRY`). A throttle by itself is retryable/benign.\n- **Exp B — the keyless-anthropic auth `TypeError` (the EXACT string recorded in session log 4f6b / inner-amiable-grebe):** `should_fall_back=False`; verdict = **INDETERMINATE** (`NEEDS_INVESTIGATION`, `exception_type=TypeError` — matches the recorded diagnostic byte-for-byte).\n- **Exp C — DECISIVE, real pydantic-ai `FallbackModel` + the real `should_fall_back` predicate:** primary raises throttle(429), fallback raises the keyless auth `TypeError`. Observed: primary attempted 1×, **failover FIRED** (fallback attempted 1×), the `TypeError` escaped the chain, final verdict = **INDETERMINATE**. This discriminates H1 (failover-to-keyless-fallback) from \"throttle alone\" (Exp A = exit 11): the failover is what converts a retryable throttle into a hard INDETERMINATE.\n\nCorroborating live evidence: session log **4f6b (inner-amiable-grebe)** records the exact incident and the operator's workaround verbatim: \"local LLM gates (review-plan/review-code/verify-completion) fail with 'Could not resolve authentication method' when Bedrock opus throttles — the frontier class falls over to a keyless anthropic fallback (no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY here). FIX: run gates with REBAR_LLM_CONFIG_FILE=$PWD/.github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml (bedrock-only, no fallback) so throttled calls retry on Bedrock.\" Plus \"6 rapid reviews likely exhausted TPM quota.\"\n\n### H2 (stale-store gate refusal) — considered and REJECTED for THIS symptom\n\nCommit 2598909d (\"Refuse gate certification on a stale store\") adds freshness checks to the CLAIM gate, the plan-review CLOSE gate, and the completion CLOSE gate, each emitting the DISTINCT verdict `freshness.STALE_VERDICT == 'stale-store'` (verified at runtime) \"before any attestation is consulted\". That is a different observable from the reported \"review-plan returns INDETERMINATE\", and it is NOT on the `review-plan` LLM verdict path (`plan_review.review-plan --status` is read-only, no LLM). Stale-store can co-occur at CLAIM time under the same concurrent-write storm, but it does not explain the reported INDETERMINATE. H1 alone explains every reported symptom (fleet-wide simultaneity via the shared account; the exact `TypeError` diagnostic; \"unsigned, no determinate verdict\").\n\n### Defect legitimacy = ESCALATE (design decision; NOT auto-fixable against an unambiguous contract)\n\nThree layers, only the third is arguably a code defect:\n1. **Operational trigger** — self-inflicted account throttle from concurrent frontier/opus fan-out (~70 worktrees). No single code defect; a load-management concern.\n2. **Environment** — `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` absent, contrary to the config's documented expectation (\"In normal local/CI operation, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is EXPECTED to be present and VALID\"). environment-or-config.\n3. **Latent disposition-masking defect** — even granting (1)+(2), the surfaced disposition is arguably WRONG: a retryable throttle is presented as a non-retryable INDETERMINATE because the chain-failure classification keeps only the TERMINAL (fallback) exception and discards the retryable PRIMARY cause. This defeats the retryable-taxonomy INTENT (`WAIT_AND_RETRY` → \"wait for the backoff window, then retry\" → exit 11). Whether to change this is a DESIGN DECISION.\n\nPer the /rebar-debug not-a-bug + design-decision guard, I STOPPED at the Phase 1 exit gate and did NOT auto-apply a fix.\n\n### Candidate remediation directions (operator's call — tradeoffs)\n\n- **(A) Operational / concurrency** — add a client-side concurrency limiter / rate-limit on frontier `review-plan` so the shared account isn't overrun (defense in depth; also cuts token spend). In-process, portable. Does not by itself fix the disposition-masking.\n- **(B) Config/env** — either ensure `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is present in agent environments (failover then succeeds transparently), OR adopt the operator's 4f6b workaround (`REBAR_LLM_CONFIG_FILE=…/bedrock.toml`, no fallback) so a throttle stays exit-11 retryable. Zero code change; per-environment.\n- **(C) Code / disposition (RECOMMENDED, see report)** — stop a throttled primary from being downgraded to INDETERMINATE by a non-retryable fallback failure. Two sub-options: (c1) exclude plain `WAIT_AND_RETRY` (rate-limit) from `should_fall_back` so a throttle RETRIES the primary instead of failing over — symmetric with the existing \"a credential error must NOT fail over\" rule and matching AWS adaptive-retry / OSS best practice for 429s; or (c2) when a `FallbackModel` chain exhausts, classify by the MOST-retryable member so a throttle+authfail group surfaces as `WAIT_AND_RETRY` (exit 11). (c1) is simpler and directly matches the operator's own conclusion.\n\n### Attribution (candidate — NOT linked pending the defect-vs-config decision)\n\nThe disposition-masking became REACHABLE when the anthropic fallback was added to the frontier chain: **`8fbd-e9d5-326e-40d8`** (commit `6d4f394195b2` \"Enable class-scoped Anthropic fallback\", 2026-08-10). Before it, frontier had NO fallback, so a throttle → `WAIT_AND_RETRY` → exit-11 retryable (no INDETERMINATE). Substrate: the failover machinery `should_fall_back` (cc33-13db-de48-4468, commit 72e59d982fee, 2026-08-02) and the closed resolution-disposition classifier (civilized-immediate-mamba, commit 4291b9a5600e, 2026-07-10). 8fbd was a DELIBERATE operator-approved decision (\"Direct Anthropic is the approved fallback for frontier and standard\"), so this is not a regression-defect; `caused_by` is intentionally NOT linked yet because whether this is a `plan_defect` vs `env_integration` disposition is part of what is being escalated. Recommended `--caused-by 8fbd-e9d5-326e-40d8` IF the operator elects the code fix (C).\n\n### Relationship to 35ab-f0e0 (fightable-nirvanic-kitten, in_progress, another agent)\n\n35ab is a SIBLING at the same classification seam but a DIFFERENT trigger: a bare `WorkflowError` (unknown scripted `uses:` step) mis-mapping to `llm_unavailable`. This incident's trigger is a provider throttle→failover→keyless-auth `TypeError`→`NEEDS_INVESTIGATION`. They share the downstream property that a non-outage condition collapses to a non-retryable verdict, but they are distinct mechanisms with distinct fixes; not duplicates. Coordinated via a note on 35ab.\n\n### Reproducer (DEBUG-rebar-debug; no real provider call)\n\n```python\nfrom rebar.llm.failure import classify_llm_failure, ClassifyContext\nfrom rebar.llm.model_classes import should_fall_back\n\ndef verdict_for(exc):\n    o = classify_llm_failure(exc, ClassifyContext(model=\"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8\"))\n    return (\"EXIT_11_RETRYABLE\" if o.retryable else \"INDETERMINATE\", o.resolution_class.value,\n            o.diagnostic.get(\"exception_type\"))\n\nfrom pydantic_ai.exceptions import ModelHTTPError\nthrottle = ModelHTTPError(status_code=429, model_name=\"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8\",\n    body={\"error\": {\"type\": \"rate_limit_error\", \"message\": \"ThrottlingException\"}})\nauth = TypeError(\"Could not resolve authentication method. Expected one of api_key, auth_token, or credentials to be set. …\")\n\n# A: should_fall_back(throttle)=True ; verdict=('EXIT_11_RETRYABLE','WAIT_AND_RETRY','ModelHTTPError')\n# B: should_fall_back(auth)=False   ; verdict=('INDETERMINATE','NEEDS_INVESTIGATION','TypeError')\n# C: real FallbackModel(primary=throttle, fallback=auth, fallback_on=should_fall_back), Agent.run(...)\n#    -> failover fires, TypeError escapes, verdict=('INDETERMINATE','NEEDS_INVESTIGATION','TypeError')\n```\n","timestamp":1788046367054894686}],"created_at":1788045211215655001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Report\n\nMultiple concurrent sessions simultaneously report `rebar review-plan` returning **INDETERMINATE** (unsigned, no determinate PASS/FAIL verdict). Sudden fleet-wide onset during a period of heavy concurrent multi-worktree activity (~70 worktrees; multiple sessions + a fanned-out batch of debug agents each running review-plan).\n\n## Observed (descriptive; not yet root-caused)\n\n- INDETERMINATE affects MULTIPLE independent sessions at once (systemic, not per-ticket).\n- Local host resources are HEALTHY: load avg ~3.5, disk 28% used, no orphaned/leaked busy-loops. So NOT local CPU/disk/leak exhaustion on this box.\n- Provider config: rebar DEFAULTS TO AWS BEDROCK (`[llm] model = bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8`, acct 896586841071/us-east-1; rebar.toml ~L145-222). Config explicitly states the chain does NOT fail over on a credential error ('a credential error must not be masked by shopping for a provider whose key happens to work'). frontier class (review-plan) = opus on Bedrock.\n- Tickets branch shows three-way divergence at report time — heavy concurrent ticket writes from many sessions.\n\n## Proven root cause (Phase 1 — H1 wins)\n\nUnder concurrent multi-session load the SHARED Bedrock account throttles at the ACCOUNT level. The frontier chain is `frontier = { model = \"bedrock:opus\", fallback = [{ model = \"anthropic:opus\" }] }`. A plain rate-limit 429 (ThrottlingException) classifies as `WAIT_AND_RETRY` (retryable), and `model_classes.should_fall_back` returns True for every retryable/`CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL` class — so a throttle fails the chain over to `anthropic:opus`. With `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` absent, the anthropic provider raises `TypeError: Could not resolve authentication method`; `should_fall_back(TypeError)` is False, so `FallbackModel` re-raises the bare `TypeError`, which `classify_llm_failure` maps to `NEEDS_INVESTIGATION` (non-retryable) → the gate emits the hard INDETERMINATE instead of the retryable exit-11. Shared account ⇒ fleet-wide simultaneity. (Full runtime proof + H2 rejection in the Phase-1 RCA comment.)\n\n## Fix plan (Phase 2 — Direction C.c1, operator-approved)\n\n**Change:** in `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py`, `should_fall_back`, EXCLUDE the `WAIT_AND_RETRY` disposition from the cross-provider failover predicate. Today it returns True for `resolution_class in _RETRYABLE ({WAIT_AND_RETRY, RETRY_NOW}) or CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL`; change it to return True only for `RETRY_NOW or CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL`. A plain Bedrock 429 account-throttle (`WAIT_AND_RETRY`) then RETRIES THE PRIMARY (Bedrock adaptive backoff, exit-11 retryable) instead of failing the frontier chain over to a keyless `anthropic:opus` whose terminal auth error masks the retryable primary cause as a hard INDETERMINATE.\n\nThis restores the pre-`8fbd` retryable-throttle disposition and EXTENDS the invariant already documented in `rebar.toml` (~L197) — \"a credential error must not be masked by shopping for a provider whose key happens to work\" — to the throttle case. `RETRY_NOW` (a down local endpoint, the case cross-provider failover genuinely exists for) and `CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL` STILL fail over. `_RETRYABLE` in `failure.py` is UNCHANGED — a throttle stays exit-11 retryable, it just no longer fails over.\n\n**Scope:** `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py` (the predicate + its docstring/import) and `tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py` (a new RED oracle asserting a throttle does not fail over, plus updating the pre-existing tests that encoded the old WAIT_AND_RETRY→failover contract). No change to `failure.py` or `rebar.toml`.\n\n**Attribution:** caused_by `8fbd-e9d5-326e-40d8` (commit `6d4f394195b2`, \"Enable class-scoped Anthropic fallback\", 2026-08-10), class `plan_defect` — its plan enabled cross-provider failover on a retryable throttle without a credential-reachable-fallback guard. Fix site (`should_fall_back`) is not the cause site (8fbd's config plan).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `should_fall_back` returns **False** for a `WAIT_AND_RETRY` failure (plain 429 rate-limit / 529 overloaded / read-timeout) — no cross-provider failover. Proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_throttle_no_failover_1c0d.py`.\n- [ ] `should_fall_back` STILL returns **True** for `RETRY_NOW` (`httpx.ConnectError`) and `CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL`, and STILL **False** for `CHANGE_SETTINGS` (401) — checked by the same `pytest` module.\n- [ ] End-to-end (mocked provider, NO real Bedrock): a throttled primary in the frontier `FallbackModel` chain does not fail over to the keyless anthropic fallback; the throttle surfaces as the exit-11 retryable disposition, NOT INDETERMINATE. Proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py`.\n- [ ] A RED oracle fails before the change and passes after; a mutation re-introducing `WAIT_AND_RETRY` into the failover set is caught (RED under `sandbox-exec`).\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` are clean; no new dependency; no test weakening.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `pytest tests/unit/test_throttle_no_failover_1c0d.py` — the held-out RED oracle (predicate + taxonomy) asserting a `WAIT_AND_RETRY` throttle does not fail over.\n- `pytest tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py` — the end-to-end failover-selection suite (updated to the new contract) + the throttle-no-failover replication.\n- `make lint` and `make typecheck` — clean.\n- Mutation check run inside `sandbox-exec -f` (the `timeout` binary is absent on this host): re-introduce `WAIT_AND_RETRY` into the failover set, confirm the oracle goes RED, restore.\n\n## Investigate/repair WITHOUT adding Bedrock load\n\nDo NOT reproduce by running live review-plan storms against Bedrock. The classification path is reproduced entirely locally with an injected/mocked provider throttle. Reported against origin/main at commit 55589c15.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py","reason":"should_fall_back: exclude WAIT_AND_RETRY from the cross-provider failover predicate (Direction C.c1) so a plain Bedrock 429 throttle retries the primary instead of failing over to a keyless anthropic fallback that masks it as INDETERMINATE."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py","reason":"New RED oracle asserting a WAIT_AND_RETRY throttle does not trigger cross-provider failover (end-to-end + predicate), plus updating the pre-existing tests that encoded the old WAIT_AND_RETRY->failover contract to the new behavior."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"b84ead0e-2479-45ac-bdcd-4b4ac4db5fbf","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"1c0d-fe83-0254-444a","ticket_type":"bug","title":"review-plan returns INDETERMINATE fleet-wide under concurrent multi-session load","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ff1aeae4-7f9a-4030-861e-fa0a19bd94cd","b84ead0e-2479-45ac-bdcd-4b4ac4db5fbf","4ddd4298-0c1c-40b5-96be-6bdeb5750284","f3259a52-0a94-404a-b018-524187294b3b","340eb6f4-552c-44be-9cab-8a464ee5cef1","776ab24b-739f-43ba-9275-3f5cd721ece3","c7c71447-8e17-4e2c-ac43-0dd63aefe33c","b03086d0-5ca9-47b7-b8a9-eb5f0ff30fb6"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788048077693139013,"uuid":"4212da31-ab74-485f-a409-492e759fd09d"}